'''Qymish nationalism''' ([[Qymish language|Qymish]]: TBD, ''TBD'') is a [[wikipedia:nationalism|nationalism]] which asserts that the [[Qymish people]] are a [[Qym|nation]] and which affirms the cultural unity of the Qymish people. From a Qymish nationalist perspective, Qymishness is defined as claiming cultural and ethnic descent from two historic peoples, the [[Byrakans]] and the [[Sukats]]. While the [[Ottelians]] have had considerable influence and have historically occupied the lands of modern-day [[Qym]], after the [[Byrakan Wars]], they usually are excluded from Qymish nationalist discourses. This is due to the association of the Ottelians with [[Prugundy]], while Qymish statesmen wanted to distance themselves from the enemy. 

